      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "2. The Wright-Fisher model extends the idea of binomial sampling to multiple generations and implies that, in a population in which the only force acting on allele frequencies is random genetic drift, the probability that an allele will drift to fixation is equal to its initial frequency in the population.",
